  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish that chemical SRO can be modeled computationally in compositionally complex BCC refractory alloys, particularly through Monte Carlo or large-cell first-principles calculations (R1, R5, R17), and that B2-like ordering, clustering, and BCC/B2 microstructural engineering are feasible in HEAs and RHEAs (R3, R4, R8, R10, R16, R20). R9 also establishes the specific HfNbTaTiZr BCC alloy as an accessible material. However, none of the records connects SRO in HfNbTaTiZr to HfTi/TiZr percolation pathways, reduced lattice-distortion scattering, altered high-frequency phonon states, or increased lattice thermal conductivity. Thus they point toward computational SRO engineering but leave the thermal-transport intervention and mechanism as a substantial new idea."
}
